r other long chain fatty acids. May modulate the arachidonic acid signaling pathway and play a role in other fatty acid signaling processes (PubMed:14660610, PubMed:24563460). May down-regulate the biological activities of N-arachidonoyl-serotonin, an endocannabinoid that has anti-nociceptive effects through inhibition of fatty acid amide hydrolase FAAH, TRPV1 receptor and T-type calcium channels. Catalyzes C-2 oxidation of the indole ring of N-arachidonoyl-serotonin forming a less active product 2-oxo-N-arachidonoyl-serotonin (PubMed:24563460)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"an omega-methyl-long-chain fatty acid + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O2 = an omega-hydroxy-long-chain fatty acid + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H2O + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:56748"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:11964"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:11965"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15379"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57618"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58210"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:140991"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:140992"}],"ecNumber":"1.14.14.80","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14660610"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24563460"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:56749"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"14660610"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"24563460"}]}]},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoate + reduced [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O2 = 19-hydroxy-(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoate + oxidized [NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H2O + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:39759"},{"datab